# Data Collection — Usage Guide

## Run order
```
config.py → 1_normal → 2_brute → 3_portscan → 4_webattack → 5_dos → 7_verify
```

## Step 1 — Edit config.py
```python
DEVSTACK_HOST = "http://192.168.x.x"   # your DevStack IP
ADMIN_PASSWORD = "..."                  # password from localrc
```

## Step 2 — Create test users (one-time setup)
```bash
source /opt/stack/openrc admin admin
for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do
  openstack user create --password test123 --project demo user$i
  openstack role add --user user$i --project demo member
done
```

## Step 3 — Run scripts in order

### Normal traffic (~45-90 minutes)
```bash
python3 1_normal_traffic.py --target 8000
```

### Brute Force (~20 minutes)
```bash
python3 2_attack_brute.py --target 2000 --mode mixed
```

### Port Scan (~15 minutes)
```bash
python3 3_attack_portscan.py --target 2000
```

### Web Attack (~30 minutes)
```bash
python3 4_attack_webattack.py --target 2000
```

### DoS (~10 minutes)
```bash
python3 5_attack_dos.py --target 2000
```

## Step 4 — Verify and merge
```bash
python3 7_verify_dataset.py
```

## Output files
```
collected_data/
├── raw_normal.csv          (8000+ rows, label=0)
├── raw_brute_mixed.csv     (2000 rows,  label=1)
├── raw_portscan.csv        (2000 rows,  label=1)
├── raw_webattack.csv       (2000 rows,  label=1)
├── raw_dos.csv             (2000 rows,  label=1)
├── final_normal.csv        (merged normal)
├── final_attack.csv        (merged attacks)
└── final_dataset.csv       (all data, shuffled)
```

## Expected statistics after collection
| Type       | Count  | fail_rate | req_rate/60s | Key signal             |
|------------|--------|-----------|--------------|------------------------|
| Normal     | 8,000  | ~5%       | 2-10         | baseline               |
| Brute      | 2,000  | ~95%      | 20-80        | high fail_rate         |
| Port Scan  | 2,000  | ~60%      | 30-100       | many unique endpoints  |
| Web Attack | 2,000  | ~70%      | 5-20         | large request_bytes    |
| DoS        | 2,000  | ~30%      | 100-300      | extreme req_rate       |

## Quick smoke test (before full collection)
```bash
python3 1_normal_traffic.py --target 50
```
If 50 rows appear in `collected_data/raw_normal.csv`, everything is working.
